---
import "../../../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
  <title>Public Surface Case — 2026-09-19</title>
  <meta name="description" content="A dated follow-up to the 2026-08-18 public surface case. The platform-field layer that specimen declined to verify has since been performed and institutionally reported. The earlier specimen is preserved unchanged; this page adds later layers and keeps them apart. External public-discourse observation, not repository evidence." />
  <style>
    :root { --deep:#15130f; --raised:#24211c; --max:920px; }
    *{box-sizing:border-box}
    html{background:var(--bg);scroll-behavior:smooth}
    body{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.7}
    a{color:var(--link);text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:3px}
    a:hover{color:var(--link-hover)}
    a:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--link);outline-offset:4px;border-radius:2px}
    h1,h2,h3{margin:0;color:var(--text);font-weight:600;line-height:1.22}
    p{margin:0}
    code{font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:var(--accent);background:transparent;padding:0}
    main{max-width:var(--max);margin:0 auto;padding:72px 24px 96px}
    .kicker,.label{font-size:.75rem;letter-spacing:.085em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .kicker{color:var(--link);margin-bottom:14px}
    .label{color:var(--muted)}

    .case-head{max-width:760px;padding-bottom:42px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .case-head h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,5vw,3.45rem);letter-spacing:-.04em;max-width:18ch;color:var(--accent)}
    .subtitle{margin-top:16px;max-width:44rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.05rem}
    .framing{margin-top:20px;max-width:42rem;font-size:1.04rem}
    .date-row{display:flex;gap:30px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:26px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem}
    .date-row span{display:block;margin-bottom:2px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .genre{margin-top:18px;padding:12px 0;border-top:1px dashed var(--line);border-bottom:1px dashed var(--line);color:var(--muted);font-size:.86rem;font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace}
    .genre b{color:var(--text);font-weight:500}

    .flow{margin:26px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.7;white-space:pre-wrap}

    .movement{scroll-margin-top:20px;padding:52px 0 8px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .movement:first-of-type{border-top:0}
    .m-num{color:var(--link);font-size:.78rem;font-weight:650;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .movement h2{margin-top:10px;max-width:34ch;font-size:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2rem);letter-spacing:-.02em}
    .movement p.lead{margin-top:14px;max-width:46rem}
    .movement p.note{margin-top:14px;max-width:46rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.95rem}
    .candidate{margin-top:8px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem;letter-spacing:.02em}
    .candidate code{color:var(--accent)}

    .reading{margin-top:22px}
    .reading-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .reading-row:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .reading-row dt{color:var(--muted);font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .reading-row dd{margin:0;max-width:46rem}
    .reading-row.reading-interpretation dd{color:var(--text)}
    .reading-row.reading-interpretation dt{color:var(--link)}
    .reading-row.reading-limit dd{color:var(--muted);font-size:.91rem}

    .distinctions{margin:18px 0 0;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px dashed var(--line);border-bottom:1px dashed var(--line);font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.85;white-space:pre-wrap}

    .gloss{margin-top:16px;padding-left:16px;border-left:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem}
    .gloss p+p{margin-top:8px}

    .not-list{margin:14px 0 0;color:var(--muted);font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.8;white-space:pre-wrap}

    .trajectory{margin-top:22px}
    .step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:150px minmax(0,1fr);gap:18px;padding:14px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .step:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
    .step dt{color:var(--accent);font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,Consolas,monospace;font-size:.82rem;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
    .step dt span{display:block;margin-top:4px;color:var(--muted);font-family:ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;font-size:.72rem;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase}
    .step dd{margin:0;max-width:46rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem}
    .step.step-institutional dd{color:var(--text)}

    .relations{margin-top:22px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px}
    .relations h3{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--link)}
    .relations ul{margin:10px 0 0;padding-left:1.05rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem}
    .relations li{margin:5px 0}
    .rel-note{margin-top:16px;max-width:46rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.82rem}

    details{margin-top:22px}
    summary{cursor:pointer;width:fit-content;color:var(--link);font-size:.85rem;font-weight:600}
    .reconstruction{margin-top:12px;padding-left:16px;border-left:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}
    .reconstruction p+p{margin-top:8px}
    .reconstruction code{color:var(--accent)}

    .sources{margin-top:22px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .source{display:grid;grid-template-columns:120px 1fr;gap:16px;padding:12px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:.86rem}
    .source strong{color:var(--link);font-weight:650}
    .source span{color:var(--muted)}
    .access{margin-top:12px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.8rem}

    .synthesis{margin-top:40px;padding-top:44px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .synthesis h2{max-width:34ch;font-size:clamp(1.4rem,3vw,2rem)}
    .one-sentence{margin-top:20px;max-width:44rem;font-size:1.06rem}
    .one-sentence strong{color:var(--text);font-weight:600}
    .boundary-note{margin-top:22px;max-width:48rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.85rem}

    footer{max-width:var(--max);margin:0 auto;padding:30px 24px 60px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted);font-size:.83rem}

    @media(max-width:760px){
      main{padding:50px 18px 74px}.case-head h1{font-size:2.2rem}
      .reading-row,.step{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px}
      .relations{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:18px}
      .source{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:3px}
    }
    @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){html{scroll-behavior:auto}}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <header class="case-head">
    <p class="kicker">Artistic Research / Public Surface Case</p>
    <h1>Semantic Casting, One Month On</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">A dated follow-up to the 2026-08-18 specimen. The earlier page is preserved unchanged; this page adds the layers that came after it and keeps them apart.</p>
    <p class="framing">On 18 August 2026 this series fixed a reading of a public-discourse field at the moment a cultural template had been cast and production elements were being proposed. That specimen declined to verify whether anything would be held. One month later the festival named in its reconstruction keywords opened, and institutional news reporting exists for it. This page records what came after the earlier reading. It revises nothing in the specimen it follows.</p>
    <div class="date-row">
      <div><span>Case date</span>19 September 2026</div>
      <div><span>Platform-field window</span>18 August – 5 September 2026, UTC+8</div>
      <div><span>Institutional window</span>18–19 September 2026, UTC+8</div>
      <div><span>Indexing</span>noindex / bounded reading</div>
    </div>
    <p class="genre"><b>Field type</b> — external public-discourse observation, follow-up layer (≠ repository evidence). <b>Status</b> — dated, verify-only case specimen; the 2026-08-18 specimen is preserved unchanged (follow-up ≠ revision; later evidence ≠ earlier error).</p>
  </header>

  <pre class="flow">dated specimen, 18 August 2026
→ platform-field layer, dated but unverified
→ an official layer forms inside the platform field
→ a warm-up performance is held, 4 September
→ institutional reporting, 18 September
→ the earlier specimen is preserved, not revised</pre>

  <section class="movement" id="held-open" aria-labelledby="ho-title">
    <div class="m-num">Movement 01</div>
    <h2 id="ho-title">What the earlier specimen held open</h2>
    <p class="lead">The <a href="/artistic-research/public-surface-case/2026-08-18/">2026-08-18 page</a> read one public-discourse field as a specimen of a general mechanism: the move from public readability toward a performable civic surface. It proposed candidate formulations and a threshold, and it was explicit about what it did not do.</p>
    <p class="note">It did not claim that any proposed performance, festival, or civic action was permitted, finalized, or held. It treated the festivalization layer as platform-field material and offered the cost threshold as a reading device, not as a property of the case. Those statements were true at their date. They remain on that page as written, because a dated specimen that is edited to match a later outcome stops being evidence of what could be read at its date.</p>
    <pre class="distinctions">follow-up ≠ revision
later evidence ≠ earlier error
a preserved specimen ≠ an endorsed specimen</pre>
  </section>

  <section class="movement" id="source-boundary" aria-labelledby="sb-title">
    <div class="m-num">Movement 02</div>
    <h2 id="sb-title">Source boundary: three layers, now four</h2>
    <p class="lead">The earlier page kept three kinds of material apart. This page adds a fourth and keeps all four apart.</p>
    <pre class="distinctions">news snapshots, August — establish only that a controversy entered public news circulation
platform-field material, 18 August – 5 September — dated screenshots held by the author; a public trace, not verification
institutional reporting, 18–19 September — establishes that the festival entered public news circulation as an event
MWE reading — an authored structural reading, not a repository or registry fact</pre>
    <dl class="reading">
      <div class="reading-row"><dt>Observed surface</dt><dd>The platform-field layer is documented by forty-five dated screenshots taken between 18 August and 5 September 2026 and held by the author. They are used here only as a reconstruction path for what was publicly posted, and when. None is reproduced on this page, and no account, name, or engagement figure is taken from them.</dd></div>
      <div class="reading-row reading-interpretation"><dt>Research reading</dt><dd>Institutional reporting changes the epistemic status of one claim only: that the event opened. It does not verify the platform-field layer retroactively. The two layers remain different kinds of evidence, and a headline that names the festival confirms nothing that was posted about it in August.</dd></div>
      <div class="reading-row reading-limit"><dt>Limit</dt><dd>The institutional layer is cited by outlet, date, headline, and URL. Article bodies are not the basis of any claim on this page. Attendance, budget, ticketing, and cash figures circulating on platforms and in other outlets vary between sources and are not adopted.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <div class="gloss">
      <p><b>Extension note (summary)</b></p>
      <p>This page is an extension layer to the 2026-08-18 case specimen, not a revision. At its date, the earlier page did not confirm that any performance or festival had been held; those boundary statements are kept as written.</p>
      <p>This page adds two layers: the platform-field layer of 18 August to 5 September (dated screenshots held by the author, used as a reconstruction path for the public trace and not reproduced on this page), and the institutional-reporting layer from 18 September (CNA, in Chinese and in English). Institutional reporting confirms only that the event entered news circulation; it does not retroactively verify any claim from the platform layer. This page does not verify attendance, budget, or ticketing figures, and it does not promote any candidate concept.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="movement" id="trajectory" aria-labelledby="tr-title">
    <div class="m-num">Movement 03</div>
    <h2 id="tr-title">A dated trajectory, read as platform-field material</h2>
    <p class="lead">What the platform-field layer shows, read at arm's length and without names, is a sequence. Each step is dated by the screenshot that records it. None is verified by this page.</p>
    <dl class="trajectory">
      <div class="step"><dt>2026-08-18<span>platform field</span></dt><dd>A proposal circulates as a joke and as a plan at once. The same day a programme with four dated nights is posted. The poster states that contracts and payments to troupes begin the next day, that the venue is not yet fixed, and that a permit question is open. Others offer food, banquet coordination, and a map edit that renames a location. One troupe issues a statement that it will evaluate professionally and not treat the performance as topic hype; a news outlet reports the schedule the same evening.</dd></div>
      <div class="step"><dt>2026-08-21<span>platform field</span></dt><dd>An official account for the festival appears. Its first statement says that an event company has been formally commissioned for planning, execution, and external information; that all information is to be taken from official pages only; and that no unauthorized person or unit represents the event. A warm-up performance is announced for 4 September at a temple in a different district. A word-mark is credited to a designer who authorized its use.</dd></div>
      <div class="step"><dt>2026-08-25 – 29<span>platform field</span></dt><dd>The programme is extended: a fifth night, additional performers, a student and folk-troupe component for one night, and a volunteer design team for the main visual. One poster is labelled by the platform as AI-generated content.</dd></div>
      <div class="step"><dt>2026-08-30<span>platform field</span></dt><dd>A second official statement draws a boundary inside the field. The festival is declared not to be a public trial of any person. On-stage content may be pointed; off-stage there is to be no personal attack, harassment, or rumour, and nothing unverified is to be treated as fact. Venue, dates, registration, and administrative information are valid only from official notices. Forwarded images, summaries, and derivative content do not represent the event.</dd></div>
      <div class="step"><dt>2026-09-04<span>platform field</span></dt><dd>The warm-up performance is held. Posts from the official account and from attendees show a full-scale outdoor puppet stage, free noodles served from a street kitchen, coins and red envelopes distributed during the opening ritual, and a large seated crowd that includes families. Attendee posts circulate widely that evening.</dd></div>
      <div class="step step-institutional"><dt>2026-09-18 – 19<span>institutional</span></dt><dd>The main festival opens in Anping, Tainan, and is reported to run five consecutive evenings. City police announce traffic control and security for it. CNA reports the opening in Chinese; its English-language service carries a report the next day.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <dl class="reading">
      <div class="reading-row"><dt>Observed surface</dt><dd>Between the first post and the first institutional report, the field acquired an official information layer, a professional intermediary, a word-mark, a design team, a boundary statement of its own, and one held performance.</dd></div>
      <div class="reading-row reading-interpretation"><dt>Research reading</dt><dd>The 2026-08-18 page proposed that a symbol changes state when it begins to absorb commitments that leave infrastructure traces. The trajectory above contains items of that kind: announced contracts, a commissioned company, a built stage, served food, a police traffic plan. Whether they establish the candidate <code>Irreversible Cost Threshold</code> as a property of this case, rather than as a reading device, is not decided here. The candidate stays a candidate.</dd></div>
      <div class="reading-row reading-limit"><dt>Limit</dt><dd>The sequence is reconstructed from screenshots taken by one observer at irregular intervals. It is not a complete record of the field, and a gap between dates is a gap in observation, not evidence of inactivity.</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="movement" id="own-boundary" aria-labelledby="ob-title">
    <div class="m-num">Movement 04</div>
    <h2 id="ob-title">The field draws its own boundary</h2>
    <p class="lead">The most legible event in the platform-field layer, for this series, is not a performance. It is that the field produced boundary statements of its own.</p>
    <p class="note">On 21 August the official layer separated itself from the crowd that had generated it: one commissioned company speaks for the event, and other voices do not. On 30 August it separated the template from its target: the festival keeps the name of a story about a punished husband while declaring that it puts no living person on trial, and it separated official notices from forwarded images, summaries, and derivative content. A field that began as distributed remix ended its first month by declaring which of its own surfaces are authoritative.</p>
    <dl class="reading">
      <div class="reading-row"><dt>Observed surface</dt><dd>A template name retained. Its literal application to a person disavowed. Official surfaces enumerated. Derivative surfaces disowned.</dd></div>
      <div class="reading-row reading-interpretation"><dt>Research reading</dt><dd>Semantic casting, as the earlier page described it, made the field readable. The boundary statements show the field managing the cost of that readability: keeping the compressed name that carries the story while refusing the reading the name most directly invites. This is offered as an observation about one field, not as a property of casting in general.</dd></div>
      <div class="reading-row reading-limit"><dt>Limit</dt><dd>Whether the disavowal was accepted by the public that read the template the other way is not observable from these materials. A boundary statement is a claim about a surface, not a measurement of how the surface was read.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <pre class="distinctions">a template name ≠ the reading it invites
an official statement ≠ an accepted boundary
a field's own boundary ≠ this page's boundary</pre>
  </section>

  <section class="movement" id="not" aria-labelledby="not-title">
    <div class="m-num">Limits</div>
    <h2 id="not-title">What this page is not</h2>
    <pre class="not-list">not a revision of the 2026-08-18 specimen
not a verification of the platform-field layer, before or after the event
not a verification of attendance, budget, ticketing, or cash figures
not an event review, a listing, or a campaign page
not a claim that the earlier reading predicted the outcome
not a promotion of any candidate concept to a Registry entry
not a moral judgment on any individual, organizer, troupe, or outlet</pre>
    <p class="note">One field, one observer's screenshots, two institutional headlines and one English-language report. That is evidence about this field in its first month, not a law about public symbols.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="movement" id="relations" aria-labelledby="rel-title">
    <div class="m-num">Relation to Meta-Writing Ecology</div>
    <h2 id="rel-title">Where this follow-up sits</h2>
    <p class="lead">This follow-up sits where the earlier specimen sits, near the artistic-research interface. It introduces no new candidate concept. The seven case-local formulations of the 2026-08-18 page are carried over with their status unchanged: not Registry entries, conferring no confirmed relation.</p>
    <div class="relations">
      <div>
        <h3>Existing surfaces (navigation-only)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="/artistic-research/public-surface-case/2026-08-18/">Semantic Casting: A Public Surface Case (2026-08-18)</a> — the specimen this page follows, preserved unchanged.</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/blob/main/false-legibility.md">False Legibility</a> — warns against treating template fit as truth.</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/blob/main/premature-circulation-model.md">Premature Circulation</a> — relevant where a form circulates before it is verified.</li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/metawritingecology/meta-writing-ecology/blob/main/reference-drift.md">Reference Drift</a> — relevant where frame and evidence drift apart.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Candidate concepts carried over (not Registry)</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Semantic Casting</li>
          <li>Cultural Compression Interface</li>
          <li>Civic Meme Materialization</li>
          <li>Irreversible Cost Threshold</li>
          <li>Distributed Vernacular Political Theatre</li>
          <li>Festivalization as Friction Reduction</li>
          <li>Ambiguity as Participation Shield</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="rel-note">These two columns are placed side by side for reading only. Co-listing is a navigation relation, not a confirmed relation, a formal dependency, or an ontology claim. The internal link to the earlier specimen is a navigation relation between two dated pages in one series; neither page is linked from site navigation. The candidate concepts remain case-local formulations pending user review.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="movement" id="sources" aria-labelledby="src-title">
    <div class="m-num">Source snapshots</div>
    <h2 id="src-title">What is cited, and what it establishes</h2>
    <p class="lead">The institutional snapshots establish only that the festival entered public news circulation as an event. The platform-field record is described, not reproduced.</p>
    <div class="sources">
      <div class="source"><strong>CNA</strong><span>2026-09-18 — “「鍘美藝術節」晚間起連5天 台南警啟動交管維安”. Police traffic control and security announced; five-evening run stated. <a href="https://www.cna.com.tw/news/aloc/202609180094.aspx">cna.com.tw/news/aloc/202609180094</a></span></div>
      <div class="source"><strong>CNA</strong><span>2026-09-18 — “鍘美藝術節一連5晚台南安平登場 首場演出「包公斬駙馬」人潮爆滿”. Opening night reported; first performance named. <a href="https://www.cna.com.tw/news/aloc/202609180288.aspx">cna.com.tw/news/aloc/202609180288</a></span></div>
      <div class="source"><strong>Focus Taiwan</strong><span>2026-09-19 — “Infidelity parable-inspired arts festival opens in Tainan”. CNA's English-language service. <a href="https://focustaiwan.tw/culture/202609190006">focustaiwan.tw/culture/202609190006</a></span></div>
      <div class="source"><strong>Platform field</strong><span>2026-08-18 to 2026-09-05 — forty-five dated screenshots of public posts on one platform and one news article read through a messaging app, held by the author. Used as a reconstruction path only. Not reproduced here; no platform image appears on this page.</span></div>
      <div class="source"><strong>Earlier specimen</strong><span>2026-08-18 — <a href="/artistic-research/public-surface-case/2026-08-18/">Semantic Casting: A Public Surface Case</a>. Preserved unchanged.</span></div>
    </div>
    <p class="access">Headlines and dates are taken from the outlets' own public listings and retained in the original language; the English report is CNA's English-language service. Article bodies are not the basis of any claim on this page. Links are event-record snapshots, not endorsements.</p>

    <details>
      <summary>Preservation note</summary>
      <div class="reconstruction">
        <p>This page does not modify the 2026-08-18 page. That page's statements that no performance, festival, or civic action was verified were true at their date and are left as written. A reader who wants the earlier reading should read it there, in its own frame, and then read this page as a later layer.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section class="synthesis" aria-labelledby="synthesis-title">
    <div class="label">One-sentence formulation</div>
    <h2 id="synthesis-title">What the follow-up holds</h2>
    <p class="one-sentence"><strong>The field that the earlier specimen declined to verify has been performed and reported, and the specimen is left as it was: the follow-up adds a layer, it does not correct a reading.</strong></p>
    <p class="boundary-note">This is a reading across one external public-discourse field, held at a second fixed date. Institutional reporting confirms that an event opened; it confirms nothing else on this page, and one observed field does not establish a system-wide law. Cultural casting remains a public-reading mechanism here, not a factual equivalence, and the candidate formulations remain candidates.</p>
  </section>
</main>
<footer>External public-discourse observation ≠ repository evidence. Later evidence ≠ earlier error. This page adds a dated layer to a dated specimen; it does not report, verify, or endorse the field it reads, and it does not revise the page it follows.</footer>
</body>
</html>
